 },
 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:08:30.876342Z",
 "text": "Under the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006* (RTA), a landlord may not enter a rental unit without written notice based on advance consent provided in a lease agreement. \n\nSection 26 governs entry without notice. Under subsection 26(1)(b), a landlord may enter without notice with the tenant's consent only if the tenant consents **at the time of entry**. Any term in a tenancy agreement attempting to circumvent statutory entry requirements is inconsistent with the Act and void.\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 26",
